10	 *
11	 * `docker compose exec` does not forward a signal to the process it started, so
12	 * cancelling or timing out a run leaves the workers alive inside the container. A
13	 * worker that is blocked between statements keeps its transaction open, and those row
14	 * locks outlive the run: the next run then fails every test on a one second lock wait
15	 * timeout, which looks like a hang but is really one stale lock.
16	 *
17	 * Only sessions that have been idle inside an open transaction past the grace period
18	 * are killed, so a healthy run's workers are never touched. Idle pooled connections
19	 * without a transaction hold no locks and are left alone.
20	 *
21	 *   php Modules/AI/scripts/reap-test-sessions.php [--grace=60]
22	 */
